            "k3b"
          ],
          "text": "search Nusa Dua family resorts"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k3d",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k3f",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k3g",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Day 7: Slow morning and departure"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k3l",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k3h",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Morning."
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k3i",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " A final swim, breakfast by the beach and easy packing. Nusa Dua is only about fifteen to twenty minutes from the airport, so you do not need a stressful early start. "
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k3j",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Travel note:"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k3k",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " still allow a comfortable buffer for traffic and family check-in, and fly home relaxed rather than rushed."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k3m",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k3n",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What to book early, and what to keep flexible"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k3s",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k3o",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Book early:"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k3p",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " your airport transfer, Bali Safari and Waterbom tickets online (cheaper than the gate), and family or connecting rooms in the July to August peak, when the good ones sell out. A private driver with child seats is worth arranging in advance, since seats are not a given. "
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k3q",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Keep flexible:"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k3r",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " beach and pool afternoons, casual warung meals, and the order of the Ubud nature stops. These are low-stakes and better decided around your kids' mood than a schedule."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k3t",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k3u",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Food and local rhythm with kids"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k3w",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k3v",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Eating out is easy. Warungs and cafes are relaxed about children, portions are generous, and rice, noodles, satay and fruit are familiar enough for fussy eaters. Eat on the early side, when places are calmer and staff have time. Drink only bottled or filtered water, including for brushing teeth, to avoid stomach upsets, and carry snacks for the gap between a late-finishing activity and dinner."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k3x",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k3y",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Mistakes families make in Bali"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k40",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k3z",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The common ones: trying to see too much and spending the holiday in the car; basing in the busy nightlife strips of central Kuta or Canggu instead of calm Sanur or Nusa Dua; underestimating the midday heat for small children; and putting kids on scooters in Bali traffic, which is a real risk. Plan one main thing a day, base somewhere gentle, and keep the afternoons free."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k41",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k42",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What to cut, adapt or upgrade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k4b",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k43",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Cut"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k44",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " an Ubud night for an extra beach night if your children are very young and happiest by the water. "
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k45",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Adapt"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k46",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " by swapping a busy attraction for a quiet beach day if the week feels too full; nobody needs both Bali Safari and Waterbom if your kids are small. "
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k47",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Upgrade"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k48",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " to a villa with a private, fenced pool, which for families is often worth more than a fancy hotel. "
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k49",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Add"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k4a",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " a couple of days for Nusa Penida or the Gili Islands only when the kids are old enough for boats and longer days."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k4c",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k4d",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Before you build this trip"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k4g",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k4e",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Best time."
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k4f",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " April to October is the dry season and the easiest weather with kids, with the calmest seas in Sanur and Nusa Dua. May, June and September are quieter than the July to August peak."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k4j",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k4h",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Visa and entry."
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k4i",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " Most nationalities get the e-VoA, valid 30 days, plus Bali's tourist levy, and both apply to children too. Fees can change, so check the latest official guidance and pay online before you fly to skip airport queues."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k4m",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k4k",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Getting around."
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k4l",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " A private driver, roughly Rp 700,000 to Rp 900,000 a day as a working estimate, is the easiest option with kids; request child seats when you book. Grab and Gojek cover short hops. Skip scooters with young children."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k4s",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "k4p",
          "_type": "affiliateLinkRef",
          "placeholderId": "AIRALO_INDONESIA"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k4n",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Money and connectivity."
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k4o",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " Cards work in hotels and larger restaurants; carry cash for warungs, markets and small entry fees. An "
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k4q",
          "marks": [
            "k4p"
          ],
          "text": "Indonesia eSIM"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k4r",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", activated before you land, keeps maps and ride apps working from the airport."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k4v",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k4t",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Health."
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k4u",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " Pack sun protection, mosquito repellent and any regular medicines. The south has good private hospitals such as BIMC and Siloam if you need them."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k4w",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k4x",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Final verdict"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k4z",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k4y",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Bali is one of the easiest places in Asia to travel with young children, but only if you resist the urge to see it all. Choose this trip if you want your kids relaxed and your days unhurried, with two calm bases and the two attractions they will actually remember. If you want more range, do not rush it into a week; come back for the Nusa islands when they are a little older, and let this trip be the gentle introduction it is built to be."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k50",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k51",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Related itineraries"
        }
      ]
    },
